# Mode one: "Search your library for a basic Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle." Bot1's library holds a Mountain (basic, not a
# Forest), a Taiga (a Forest, but not basic) and a Forest: only the Forest may be found (refusals for the first two). It arrives tapped. Bot1's graveyard holds no
# Cave card, so the second mode has no target and cannot be chosen (`! Modes(2)`); the first is the positive control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Glimpse the Core
Island
Island
Island
Mountain
Taiga
Forest
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glimpse the Core.Cast
! Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Modes(1)
! Bot1.Search(Mountain)
! Bot1.Search(Taiga)
Bot1.Search(Forest)

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Glimpse the Core
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Tapped = true
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
